{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/544821-the-lifespan-and-number-of-the-created","id":544821,"title":"the lifespan and number of the Created","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T22:41:44-07:00","id":544821,"title":"the lifespan and number of the Created","content":"Hey guys, I have a few questions regarding a Prommie's age and number.<br /> <br /> First, doo The Created have a definite lifespan? I know somebody told me that the Created have to be careful with their inner fires, that they must become a more stable form, a being with a human soul, before their Azoth burns them from within. Does that mean that a Created that has spend years, perhaps centuries on the Pilgrimage and a high Azoth rating is in danger of taking damage? <br /> <br /> Does going to the wastes to lower their Azoth puts more time back up on their lifespan?<br /> <br /> Secondly, are Prometheans still the racist among the supernaturals? (Course I might argue that Mummies are pretty few in number too.) Keep in mind, there are entire secret mortal alchemist societies that have sprang up from their interactions with Prometheans. Therefore, with them hunting them down, there should be a larger amount of Created or else they would quickly go extinct.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:57:45-07:00","id":544842,"title":"","content":"As I understand, a cautious Promethean is functionally immortal. They can be slain, but as long as they remember to go to the wastes every so often, they can live for centuries. Mr. Verney, for example, was the original Frankenstein's Monster, and he was created in the early 1800's.<br /> <br /> And as far as rarity, it's implied that they are indeed quite rare, seeing as in Mortal Remains, they specifically note that even knowledgeable organizations like the Loyalists of Thule and TFV know very little about them. I'd go so far as to guess there's only a couple hundred of them at the <i>absolute</i> most? I heard an estimate of about 100, but I cant recall where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:58:15-07:00","id":545365,"title":"","content":"In 1e, at least, Prometheans had a set number of years before their Azoth burned out. However, if they went to the waste and rested there for a stretch of years, they could reset their clock and live a long time. In a way, this is like vampires and torpor - every once in a while, you need a rest to reset yourself. So, yes, they functionally have an infinite life span.<br /> <br /> As for rarity? Thematically, they're still very rare compared to others, but exact numbers of supernaturals are still up to individual STs. There's no way to tell how many Mummies there are, and there very well be more than the few hundred Prommies in the one book. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:24:05-07:00","id":546573,"title":"","content":"The resurrection process also adds time to the clock, so the nepri and those who've learned their trick also have an easier time lasting longer.<br /> <br /> There's also a rumour in a book that lineage founders might be literally immortal- Varney might be joined by far older sibling such as Osiris, Galatea, and Tammuz, when it comes to founders still being around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}